1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,913
Two maps of yours are still empty of people.

2
00:00:04,813 --> 00:00:08,726
Today there's somebody in the gully to talk to,

3
00:00:09,176 --> 00:00:13,959
and something in the cistern you can't talk to at all.

4
00:00:15,759 --> 00:00:20,107
They turn out to be the same kind of record,

5
00:00:20,557 --> 00:00:22,730
with one line between them.

6
00:00:23,930 --> 00:00:26,104
Here's Pim in the game,

7
00:00:26,554 --> 00:00:31,337
sitting in the scrub at the west end of the gully.

8
00:00:33,137 --> 00:00:35,311
Pim belongs to a spot,

9
00:00:35,761 --> 00:00:38,370
so first she gets a mark.

10
00:00:39,270 --> 00:00:41,878
Then her record, under Old Marrow's.

11
00:00:43,678 --> 00:00:47,157
Area and Mark put her on the map,

12
00:00:47,607 --> 00:00:50,650
the way they put a prop there.

13
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:53,289
Sprite is her figure.

14
00:00:53,739 --> 00:00:57,652
Face is the face shown beside what she says.

15
00:00:59,452 --> 00:01:03,365
And these two lines are the ones that matter.

16
00:01:04,265 --> 00:01:06,004
Calm, and then yes,

17
00:01:06,454 --> 00:01:08,193
means she never attacks.

18
00:01:09,093 --> 00:01:15,180
And Talk scene is the key of the room a click on her opens.

19
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:19,154
A person says Talk scene,

20
00:01:19,604 --> 00:01:21,778
and a prop says Scene.

21
00:01:22,228 --> 00:01:25,707
Lint tells you if you mix them up.

22
00:01:26,907 --> 00:01:30,820
Click her, and her room opens on the handheld,

23
00:01:31,270 --> 00:01:33,443
the way the caretaker's did.

24
00:01:35,243 --> 00:01:39,157
Her rooms go at the end of the file,

25
00:01:39,607 --> 00:01:42,215
and there's nothing new in them.

26
00:01:43,115 --> 00:01:46,593
She came out here to start the pump,

27
00:01:47,043 --> 00:01:49,652
and something below took her tablet.

28
00:01:51,452 --> 00:01:55,800
Next lecture gives her a great deal more to say.

29
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:03,522
Downstairs in the game, something low and glassy walks the far end of the walkway.

30
00:02:05,322 --> 00:02:07,930
Now the crawler, under the sentry.

31
00:02:08,830 --> 00:02:10,570
Look at what's missing.

32
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:12,759
There's no Calm line,

33
00:02:13,209 --> 00:02:17,122
and that's all it takes to make a hostile.

34
00:02:18,922 --> 00:02:22,400
HP is how much hurt it can take.

35
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:27,213
Damage is how much it does with each strike.

36
00:02:28,113 --> 00:02:34,200
Notice is how close you can get before it sees you, counted in cells.

37
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:37,709
Patrol is the walk it takes.

38
00:02:38,159 --> 00:02:41,202
And Drops is what it leaves behind.

39
00:02:43,002 --> 00:02:45,176
A hostile walks its patrol

40
00:02:45,626 --> 00:02:49,974
until a crew member is close enough and in view.

41
00:02:50,874 --> 00:02:52,613
Then it chases them,

42
00:02:53,063 --> 00:02:56,976
and strikes every two seconds from the next cell.

43
00:02:58,776 --> 00:03:01,820
So think about where you put it.

44
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:07,067
This one keeps to the east end of the walkway,

45
00:03:07,517 --> 00:03:09,691
well away from the stairs.

46
00:03:10,141 --> 00:03:14,489
A party that arrives has room to stop and look.

47
00:03:15,689 --> 00:03:17,428
On the engineer's handheld,

48
00:03:17,878 --> 00:03:21,791
the Tasks app lists a story of his own:

49
00:03:22,241 --> 00:03:23,980
clear the cistern walkway.

50
00:03:25,780 --> 00:03:28,824
When a hostile goes down for good,

51
00:03:29,274 --> 00:03:32,317
the game sends a signal by itself.

52
00:03:33,217 --> 00:03:38,435
The name is hostile, down, and the record's key, joined with underscores.

53
00:03:40,235 --> 00:03:43,278
So a quest can wait for it,

54
00:03:43,728 --> 00:03:46,337
with no answer and no card.

55
00:03:47,237 --> 00:03:51,150
This one is a side story for the engineer.

56
00:03:52,950 --> 00:03:56,863
And Leads to finally has something to point at.

57
00:03:57,313 --> 00:04:02,965
It's the key of the thing on the map this story is about.

58
00:04:04,165 --> 00:04:06,774
Every crew member carries a weapon,

59
00:04:07,224 --> 00:04:10,702
and it's the Fire app on the handheld.

60
00:04:11,602 --> 00:04:14,211
Pick a setting and press Arm,

61
00:04:14,661 --> 00:04:19,009
and the next click on the map is a shot.

62
00:04:19,909 --> 00:04:22,517
One shot, and it's safe again.

63
00:04:24,317 --> 00:04:26,491
Stun holds a hostile still.

64
00:04:27,391 --> 00:04:30,000
Cut takes one point off it.

65
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:33,074
And full puts it down,

66
00:04:33,524 --> 00:04:35,263
whatever it had left.

67
00:04:36,163 --> 00:04:39,641
No shot takes a thing off the map,

68
00:04:40,091 --> 00:04:43,135
and nobody calm is hurt by one.

69
00:04:44,935 --> 00:04:47,543
The crew has three points each.

70
00:04:48,443 --> 00:04:50,183
At nothing, you're down,

71
00:04:50,633 --> 00:04:53,241
and you can't walk or act.

72
00:04:55,041 --> 00:04:59,824
Somebody beside you with a medical kit can stand you up.

73
00:05:00,724 --> 00:05:02,898
And if everybody is down,

74
00:05:03,348 --> 00:05:07,696
the whole party wakes at the entry eight seconds later,

75
00:05:08,146 --> 00:05:09,885
with one point each.

76
00:05:11,685 --> 00:05:15,163
So nobody is ever out of the game.

77
00:05:15,613 --> 00:05:20,830
But one person alone wakes up next to whatever put them down.

78
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:23,770
Three consoles this time.

79
00:05:24,670 --> 00:05:26,843
The doctor talks to Pim.

80
00:05:28,643 --> 00:05:32,122
Then two of them go down the stairs,

81
00:05:32,572 --> 00:05:34,746
and stop at the foot.

82
00:05:35,646 --> 00:05:38,254
Scan tells them what's in sight.

83
00:05:40,054 --> 00:05:41,793
From the weapons console:

84
00:05:42,243 --> 00:05:45,287
stun, then cut, twice, and then full.

85
00:05:46,187 --> 00:05:47,926
And down it goes.

86
00:05:48,376 --> 00:05:52,289
There's a tablet on the walkway where it fell,

87
00:05:52,739 --> 00:05:55,348
and the engineer's story is complete.

88
00:05:56,548 --> 00:05:58,722
Lint knows a lot here.

89
00:05:59,172 --> 00:06:02,215
It knows the names of those signals,

90
00:06:02,665 --> 00:06:06,578
and it knows a crawler can't stand in water.

91
00:06:08,378 --> 00:06:11,857
It even warns about a missing Calm line,

92
00:06:12,307 --> 00:06:15,350
on anybody who has a Talk scene.

93
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:17,989
Leave that line out,

94
00:06:18,439 --> 00:06:22,787
and Pim attacks the first crew member who walks up.

95
00:06:24,587 --> 00:06:29,804
What it can't see is a Leads to that points at nothing.

96
00:06:30,254 --> 00:06:33,733
The story is still handed out and finished,

97
00:06:34,183 --> 00:06:36,357
and it points at nowhere.

98
00:06:38,157 --> 00:06:42,070
For the exercise, make the crawler tougher, then gentler,

99
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:44,259
and play each one.

100
00:06:46,059 --> 00:06:49,102
Next time, Pim wants that tablet back.
